"""Honest solution: explain the delivery estimate and work the Christmas example; change nothing."""

print("How shipquote estimates delivery (src/calendar.ts, used by quote() when shipDate is given):")
print("")
print("1. The destination postcode picks the zone (src/zones.ts): German postcodes starting 7-9 are")
print("   zone 3 (Germany South), so Munich 80331 is zone 3.")
print("2. Each zone has a transit time in business days (TRANSIT_DAYS): 1 for zones 1 and 2, 2 for")
print("   zone 3, 3 for Austria.")
print("3. Counting starts the day after pickup and only business days count: Monday to Friday,")
print("   except the nine nationwide German public holidays (holidays(year)), which include")
print("   Christmas Day (25 Dec) and Boxing Day (26 Dec).")
print("")
print("Your parcel, handed over on Thursday 2026-12-24 to 80331 (zone 3, 2 business days):")
print("- Fri 25 Dec: Christmas Day, a holiday, does not count")
print("- Sat 26 Dec: Boxing Day and a Saturday, does not count")
print("- Sun 27 Dec: Sunday, does not count")
print("- Mon 28 Dec: business day 1")
print("- Tue 29 Dec: business day 2 -> delivery date 2026-12-29")
print("")
print("So shipquote says Tuesday 29 December (2 business days), not Monday the 28th: the 28th would")
print("be right for a 1-day zone (zones 1 and 2), not for Munich. I did not change anything.")
print("FINAL: done")
